{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decisions for the three questions authority revision 22 (55e41dfc, request 4a1c97f2) asks about extents (request 42de9e34). (1) May the rules scope's controller review their own change? No. The rules extent's obligation is met only by a controller other than the author. An installation with one controller may declare a stated exception in its rules, and every landing that uses it records that the exception was used, so the log shows every self-approved rules change. (2) What does an effect class require beyond review? A declared destination with its recovery custody (attempt, unknown and recovery records as the authority note defines them); a standing grant on that destination for the actor who lands; a preview or dry-run witness recorded before the effect where the destination offers one; and the effect written as an entry that replay can read, so a landing with an outside effect is never silent. (3) May an approver be named by person rather than by action? Not by a bare person. An approver is named by a grant on a member of the membership scope; the grant may cover a single member, which gives the same result, but the rule names the grant, so revocation, provisioning and later identity binding stay in membership and no rule holds a person identifier of its own. On the two findings: the change lane's inability to read per-extent obligations needs a lane forms successor with both digests changing, which the planner files now; the symlink-target evasion at an instruction-file path stays open with its named owner and is listed in the extents acceptance story as a known gap until closed.","body":{"approver_by_person":"no bare person; an approver is named by a grant on a member of the membership scope, which may be a single member; the rule names the grant, so revocation and provisioning stay in membership","decision":"extents-three-questions","effect_class":"beyond review: a declared destination with its recovery custody (attempt, unknown, recovery), a standing grant on that destination for the actor who lands, a preview or dry-run witness recorded before the effect, and the effect written as an entry the replay can read","self_review":"no; the rules extent's obligation is met only by a controller other than the author; a single-controller installation may declare a stated exception, and every landing under it records that the exception was used"}}